d":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-04-02T20:40:38Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T08:27:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935]\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu, Wayland\n\n### Issue description\n\nthe expected behavior of the BaseButton `pressed` signal is to be fired on key up.\n\nwhen focused and pressing an `ui_accept` mapped key, the pressed signal fires on key up.\n\nwhen clicking on it with LMB, the pressed signal fires on key up.\n\nonly when setting a shortcut `InputEvent*`, it is suddenly on key down.\n\nmost input events have a `pressed` property to indicate this state, however, this is entirely ignored by the shortcut.\n\nthis is a problem as when your pressed logic sometimes runs earlier than expected, it easily messes up other logic.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nsee MRP\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot_4_shortcut_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26448380/godot_4_shortcut_bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118133/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118133/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}